This directory holds all the of the scripts related to the hubSpace hub upload feature.

The main components are:
tusd/ - holds everything run by admins to have the file transfer daemon
    running, including cleaning up statle files. These are cronjobs ran by the
    admins so don't modify them without also changing the admin ran copy. Note there are copies for both the hgwdev version and the RR version

measure/ - the scripts that measure the state of the hubspace file system and
    output stats for viewing over time
    measureHubSpace.sh - production copy, run as qateam on the hubspace machine,
        writes /home/qateam/hubSpace/YYYY/MM/YYYY-MM-DDTHH.txt
    measureHubSpace.dev.sh - hgwdev copy, writes ~/hubSpace/YYYY/MM/YYYY-MM-DDTHH.txt
    hubSpaceReport.py - reads all of those dated reports and writes one HTML
        page of charts (storage, files and users over time, storage by file
        format) for management.  Usage:
            hubSpaceReport.py [-l label] logDir outFile.html
    hubSpaceReport.css, hubSpaceReport.js - the styles and drawing code shared
        by every page hubSpaceReport.py writes.  The pages load them from their
        own directory, so copy both into ~chmalee/public_html/hubSpace/ when
        they change.
    measureHubSpaceWrapper*.bash - the weekly cron wrappers, one per machine.
        Each runs the measure script and then hubSpaceReport.py.  The hgwdev
        page goes to ~chmalee/public_html/hubSpace/hgwdev.html.  The production
        page is written to /home/qateam/hubSpace/production.html on the
        hubspace machine, and a cron job on hgwdev copies it next to the
        hgwdev page.
